---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';
const site = siteFromHost();
const path = "/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-mailchimp";
const title = "Yotpo Email & SMS to Mailchimp: Shopify migration decisions";
const desc = "Evaluate Mailchimp for the audiences and Shopify campaigns you actually maintain, while handling retained Yotpo products and channel needs separately.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Must I leave Mailchimp at a certain order volume?",
    "answer": "No. Evaluate the required data, automations, channels and operating costs. Order volume alone does not establish that Mailchimp needs replacement."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does Shopify sync restore old Yotpo consent history?",
    "answer": "Do not assume that it does. Use consent and suppression evidence you can access, and resolve missing history before marking imported records as marketable."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
    <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a></nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p></header>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>The comparison has become a migration decision</h2>
      <p>Yotpo Email & SMS is retired. Its live lifecycle notice says the dashboard and associated background services are inactive. Keeping Yotpo Reviews or Loyalty does not restore messaging. Evaluate a replacement sender while treating those retained products as separate services; the old suite-versus-standalone recommendation no longer describes an available choice.</p>
      <h2>Map store buyers to the right audience</h2>
      <p>Mailchimp documents a Shopify connection for customer and order data. The useful decision is whether its audience model fits the store and any existing newsletter program. Identify signup sources, subscription preferences and purchaser exclusions before import. A recipe newsletter subscriber, a wholesale buyer and a gift purchaser can require different messages even if all appear in the same store. Recreate those distinctions with available fields rather than imposing an order-count graduation rule.</p>
      <h2>Preserve the editorial workflow that already works</h2>
      <p>For a team using Mailchimp for newsletters as well as store promotions, familiar campaign editing can be a practical benefit. Rehearse a product announcement and a non-product newsletter, inspecting mobile layout, product destinations and audience selection. If the team can maintain both safely, growth alone is not a reason to leave. If a required event or exclusion cannot be represented, document that gap and compare alternatives around that named requirement.</p>
      <h2>Separate review collection from promotional email</h2>
      <p>Moving messaging to Mailchimp does not require removing Yotpo Reviews from product pages. Keep review collection with an identified active owner unless a supported replacement is configured. Do not assume Shopify order sync includes reviewer status or loyalty balance. Establish a documented data route before targeting non-reviewers or inserting points in a Mailchimp message. Without that route, keep those claims and branches out of the campaign.</p>
      <h2>Rebuild seasonality without invented performance claims</h2>
      <p>A gift-led shop may need reminders around a relevant occasion rather than routine replenishment. Draft the segment from purchase information that is actually available and distinguish the buyer from the recipient. For recovery, rehearse a completed purchase and inspect pending follow-up. The earlier merchant anecdotes, submission-rate comparisons and claims that Mailchimp becomes inadequate at a particular monthly revenue were unsupported; workflow acceptance should use the store’s own records.</p>
      <h2>Confirm SMS scope and current costs independently</h2>
      <p>Do not assume an email migration also moves sender registration, SMS consent or every destination country. Confirm Mailchimp channel availability and requirements for the intended program before choosing a combined stack. Request current terms for the audience, plan and sends you need, including seasonal peaks. Add retained Yotpo services and migration work to the budget. No fixed savings estimate or mandatory quarter-long trial follows from this comparison.</p>
      <h2>Reconstruct the program from accessible records</h2>
      <p>Start with prior exports, saved templates, consent evidence, suppression records and Shopify data you can legitimately access. Do not promise a fresh export from the retired Yotpo dashboard. Ask support what recovery remains possible before setting a launch date. A customer email or phone number in an order record does not establish marketing permission. Preserve opt-outs and mark unknown consent for review rather than importing every customer as subscribed.</p>
      <h2>Activate against a message ownership map</h2>
      <p>List welcome, cart, checkout recovery, post-purchase education, review collection, loyalty notices and winback separately. Prepare replacement messages disabled and inspect purchase exits, opt-outs and missing fields before activation. Give each trigger one live owner, including Shopify automations and retained Yotpo modules. Record who can pause each sender if a customer receives the wrong sequence. These are proposed acceptance exercises, not tests we ran or evidence of revenue lift.</p>
      <h2>Primary sources</h2>
      <p>Product information checked November 25, 2026. <a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Yotpo lifecycle notice</a> · <a class="link" href="https://mailchimp.com/help/connect-shopify/">Mailchimp Shopify connection</a></p>
    </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-mailchimp">Omnisend vs Mailchimp</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-omnisend">Yotpo vs Omnisend</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/food-and-beverage">Email apps for food & beverage</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/welcome-series">Welcome series playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Migration questions" />
</BaseLayout>
